# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rotate bosonic modes {#rotate-bosonic-modes}"
msgstr "I-rotate ang mga bosonic mode {#rotate-bosonic-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") mixes bosonic modes with a unitary matrix $U$, as a network of beamsplitters and phase shifters does. It is called **passive** because it conserves the total boson number: it moves bosons between modes and never creates or destroys one. (Squeezing and displacement are the *active* operations, and a mode rotation cannot express them.) It maps the creation operators as\n"
msgstr "Hinahalo ng isang [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") ang mga bosonic mode gamit ang unitary matrix na $U$, tulad ng ginagawa ng network ng mga beamsplitter at phase shifter. Tinatawag itong **passive** dahil pinapanatili nito ang kabuuang bilang ng boson: naglilipat ito ng mga boson sa pagitan ng mga mode at hindi kailanman lumilikha o sumisira ng isa. (Ang squeezing at displacement ay ang mga *active* na operasyon, at hindi ito kayang ipahayag ng mode rotation.) Ina-map nito ang mga creation operator bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b^\\dagger_i \\mapsto \\sum_j U_{ji} \\, b^\\dagger_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b^\\dagger_i \\mapsto \\sum_j U_{ji} \\, b^\\dagger_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which on the full Fock space is the many-body unitary\n"
msgstr "na sa buong Fock space ay ang many-body unitary na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\exp\\left(\\sum_{ij} \\log(U)_{ij} \\, b^\\dagger_i b_j\\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\exp\\left(\\sum_{ij} \\log(U)_{ij} \\, b^\\dagger_i b_j\\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the gate behind a linear-optical interferometer: send Fock states in, rotate the modes, and read out how the bosons redistribute. Like every gate of a [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), it carries no truncation and no encoding. Both enter at transpile time, and this guide shows why the truncation needs particular care for a rotation.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang gate sa likod ng isang linear-optical interferometer: magpadala ng mga Fock state, i-rotate ang mga mode, at basahin kung paano muling naipamahagi ang mga boson. Tulad ng bawat gate ng isang [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") (tingnan ang [Gumamit ng mga bosonic circuit](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), wala itong dalang truncation at walang encoding. Pareho silang pumapasok sa oras ng transpile, at ipinapakita ng gabay na ito kung bakit nangangailangan ng espesyal na pag-iingat ang truncation para sa isang rotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a rotation {#build-a-rotation}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng rotation {#build-a-rotation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constructor takes the $M \\times M$ unitary matrix. The gate acts on $M$ modes. The class does not check that the matrix is unitary, so that is your responsibility.\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha ng constructor ang $M \\times M$ na unitary matrix. Kumikilos ang gate sa $M$ na mga mode. Hindi sinusuri ng class kung unitary ang matrix, kaya iyon ay responsibilidad mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common rotations have dedicated constructors. [`ModeRotation.beamsplitter()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.beamsplitter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.beamsplitter\") takes a mixing angle $\\theta$ and an optional phase $\\phi$, and $\\theta = \\pi/4$ gives the balanced 50:50 beamsplitter. [`ModeRotation.phase_shift()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.phase_shift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.phase_shift\") takes one phase per mode.\n"
msgstr "May mga nakalaang constructor ang mga karaniwang rotation. Ang [`ModeRotation.beamsplitter()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.beamsplitter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.beamsplitter\") ay kumukuha ng mixing angle na $\\theta$ at opsyonal na phase na $\\phi$, at ang $\\theta = \\pi/4$ ay nagbibigay ng balanseng 50:50 na beamsplitter. Ang [`ModeRotation.phase_shift()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.phase_shift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.phase_shift\") ay kumukuha ng isang phase kada mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also start from the anti-Hermitian generator $K$ and let the gate exponentiate it, which gives the rotation $\\exp(K)$. The generator is recovered with [`generator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.generator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.generator\").\n"
msgstr "Puwede ka ring magsimula sa anti-Hermitian na generator na $K$ at hayaan ang gate na i-exponentiate ito, na nagbibigay ng rotation na $\\exp(K)$. Nakukuha muli ang generator gamit ang [`generator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.generator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.generator\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bridge to the operator algebra is [`to_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator\"), which returns the Hermitian generator $H = \\sum_{ij} \\mathrm{i} \\log(U)_{ij} \\, b^\\dagger_i b_j$ as a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\"), so that the gate is $e^{-\\mathrm{i} H}$. For the 50:50 beamsplitter, that is a pair of hopping terms with opposite imaginary coefficients. The operator is Hermitian, which is what an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate needs, and it conserves the particle number.\n"
msgstr "Ang tulay papunta sa operator algebra ay ang [`to_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator\"), na nagbabalik ng Hermitian na generator na $H = \\sum_{ij} \\mathrm{i} \\log(U)_{ij} \\, b^\\dagger_i b_j$ bilang isang [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\"), kaya ang gate ay $e^{-\\mathrm{i} H}$. Para sa 50:50 na beamsplitter, isa itong pares ng mga hopping term na may magkabilang imaginary na coefficient. Hermitian ang operator, na siyang kailangan ng isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, at pinapanatili nito ang bilang ng particle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term reads `(is_creation, mode)` from left to right, so the second one is $\\mathrm{i} \\tfrac{\\pi}{4} \\, b^\\dagger_1 b_0$.\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ang bawat term bilang `(is_creation, mode)` mula kaliwa pakanan, kaya ang pangalawa ay $\\mathrm{i} \\tfrac{\\pi}{4} \\, b^\\dagger_1 b_0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Act on Fock states {#act-on-fock-states}"
msgstr "Kumilos sa mga Fock state {#act-on-fock-states}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A rotation moves bosons between modes, so its effect is easiest to see on Fock states. The Hong-Ou-Mandel effect is the standard example. Send one boson into each input mode of a balanced beamsplitter. The two paths that leave the bosons in different output modes interfere destructively, so the state $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ disappears and the bosons always leave together, in $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ or $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, each with probability one half.\n"
msgstr "Naglilipat ng mga boson sa pagitan ng mga mode ang isang rotation, kaya pinakamadaling makita ang epekto nito sa mga Fock state. Ang Hong-Ou-Mandel effect ang karaniwang halimbawa. Magpadala ng isang boson sa bawat input mode ng balanseng beamsplitter. Ang dalawang landas na nag-iiwan sa mga boson sa magkaibang output mode ay nag-i-interfere nang destructive, kaya nawawala ang estadong $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ at laging magkasamang umaalis ang mga boson, sa $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ o $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, bawat isa ay may probability na kalahati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the circuit on bosonic modes and lower it with the preset pass manager. The [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") fixes the truncation and the encoding at this point. A cutoff of `max_occupation=2` keeps the levels 0, 1, and 2 of every mode.\n"
msgstr "Buuin ang circuit sa mga bosonic mode at ibaba ito gamit ang preset pass manager. Itinatakda ng [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") ang truncation at ang encoding sa puntong ito. Ang cutoff na `max_occupation=2` ay nagtatago ng mga level 0, 1, at 2 ng bawat mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pipeline returns an ordinary qubit circuit. Read the outcome probabilities from the final state, here with Qiskit’s [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector), which is exact at this size. Any simulator that returns amplitudes or counts works. A Fock state $\\lvert n_0, n_1 \\rangle$ is a single computational basis state, whose index is given by the bit patterns of [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\"); the second mode’s qubits follow the first mode’s.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabalik ang pipeline ng ordinaryong qubit circuit. Basahin ang mga outcome probability mula sa huling estado, dito gamit ang [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) ng Qiskit, na eksakto sa laking ito. Gumagana ang anumang simulator na nagbabalik ng mga amplitude o count. Ang isang Fock state na $\\lvert n_0, n_1 \\rangle$ ay iisang computational basis state, na ang index ay ibinibigay ng mga bit pattern ng [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\"); sumusunod ang mga qubit ng pangalawang mode sa mga qubit ng una.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ outcome has probability zero, and the two bunched outcomes share the probability equally.\n"
msgstr "Zero ang probability ng outcome na $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$, at pantay na naghahati ang dalawang bunched na outcome sa probability.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the cutoff {#choose-the-cutoff}"
msgstr "Piliin ang cutoff {#choose-the-cutoff}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous result needs `max_occupation=2`. Run the same circuit with a cutoff of 1. That is enough to hold the input state $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$, but not the state that the rotation produces from it, which has weight on $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ and $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng naunang resulta ang `max_occupation=2`. Patakbuhin ang parehong circuit na may cutoff na 1. Sapat iyon para hawakan ang input state na $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$, pero hindi ang estadong nililikha ng rotation mula rito, na may bigat sa $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ at $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit runs without any error, and the answer is wrong: the state stays at $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ with probability one. A rotation mixes occupation sectors *within* a mode. Two bosons can end up in the same output mode, so the exact state has weight on occupation 2 in a mode that started with one boson. With a cutoff of 1 that level does not exist, and the truncated generator cannot move the state there.\n"
msgstr "Tumatakbo ang circuit nang walang anumang error, at mali ang sagot: nananatili ang estado sa $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ na may probability na isa. Hinahalo ng rotation ang mga occupation sector *sa loob* ng isang mode. Puwedeng mapunta ang dalawang boson sa iisang output mode, kaya ang eksaktong estado ay may bigat sa occupation 2 sa mode na nagsimula sa isang boson. Sa cutoff na 1, hindi umiiral ang level na iyon, at hindi maililipat ng na-truncate na generator ang estado roon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A bound on the occupation of the initial state is therefore not enough. The cutoff must cover the total boson number that can reach **any single mode** of the rotation. For $N$ bosons in total, the safe choice is a cutoff of $N$.\n"
msgstr "Kaya hindi sapat ang bound sa occupation ng paunang estado. Dapat sakop ng cutoff ang kabuuang bilang ng boson na puwedeng makarating sa **anumang iisang mode** ng rotation. Para sa $N$ na boson sa kabuuan, ang ligtas na pagpili ay cutoff na $N$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same reasoning applies to every mode separately, so a mix of different cutoffs per mode (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)) makes a rotation easy to map incorrectly. A mode that can receive bosons needs a cutoff that covers what it can receive, not only what it holds initially. The check [`LevelSpec.truncation()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec.truncation \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec.truncation\") compares a spec with the occupation lower bound of an operator. It cannot flag the case above. Each term of the beamsplitter generator holds a single creation operator, so the bound is one and the check reports no shortfall at a cutoff of 1, although the result there is wrong:\n"
msgstr "Nalalapat ang parehong pangangatwiran sa bawat mode nang hiwalay, kaya ang halo ng magkakaibang cutoff kada mode (tingnan ang [Ilarawan ang truncation gamit ang LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)) ay nagpapadali ng maling pag-map ng isang rotation. Ang mode na puwedeng tumanggap ng mga boson ay nangangailangan ng cutoff na sumasakop sa kaya nitong tanggapin, hindi lang sa hawak nito sa simula. Ikinukumpara ng check na [`LevelSpec.truncation()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec.truncation \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec.truncation\") ang isang spec sa lower bound ng occupation ng isang operator. Hindi nito matutukoy ang kaso sa itaas. Ang bawat term ng beamsplitter generator ay may hawak na iisang creation operator, kaya ang bound ay isa at walang iniuulat na kakulangan ang check sa cutoff na 1, kahit mali ang resulta roon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A further caution follows from the way the transpiler builds a rotation (next section). It applies the rotation as a sequence of two-mode factors, and the plugin documentation warns that a single factor can populate a level that the complete rotation never reaches. The truncated sequence and the truncated single evolution are then different approximations of the same unitary. A search over 1,080 random three-mode rotations, with one boson in each of two input modes and no double occupation in the output, did not turn up such a case, so treat this as a precaution and not as a common failure. Converge the cutoff as you would for any other circuit, by increasing it until the result stops changing.\n"
msgstr "May isa pang babala na nagmumula sa paraan ng pagbuo ng transpiler ng rotation (susunod na seksyon). Inilalapat nito ang rotation bilang sunud-sunod na two-mode na mga factor, at binabalaan ng dokumentasyon ng plugin na ang isang factor ay puwedeng magpuno ng level na hindi kailanman naaabot ng kumpletong rotation. Magkaibang approximation ng parehong unitary ang na-truncate na sequence at ang na-truncate na iisang evolution. Ang paghahanap sa 1,080 na random na three-mode rotation, na may isang boson sa bawat isa sa dalawang input mode at walang double occupation sa output, ay hindi nakahanap ng ganoong kaso, kaya ituring ito bilang pag-iingat at hindi karaniwang pagkabigo. I-converge ang cutoff gaya ng gagawin mo sa anumang ibang circuit, sa pamamagitan ng pagtaas nito hanggang tumigil sa pagbabago ang resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How the transpiler synthesizes a rotation {#how-the-transpiler-synthesizes-a-rotation}"
msgstr "Paano sini-synthesize ng transpiler ang isang rotation {#how-the-transpiler-synthesizes-a-rotation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `optimization` stage of the preset pipeline breaks a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") down in bosonic space first, with the [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") pass and the [`BosonicClementsDecomposition`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-clements-decomposition#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicClementsDecomposition \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicClementsDecomposition\") method (registered as `ModeRotation.Clements`). That is a choice of the preset and not a requirement of the framework: a later section lowers the same gate without any decomposition. The decomposition does not exponentiate the full generator in one step. It first factorizes the unitary into at most $M(M-1)/2$ rotations between *adjacent* modes plus $M$ single-mode phases, following the rectangular mesh of Clements et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id2). Each factor becomes an atomic [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, which the boson-to-qubit stage maps like any other.\n"
msgstr "Ang yugto ng `optimization` ng preset pipeline ay naghahati muna sa isang [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") sa bosonic space, gamit ang pass na [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") at ang method na [`BosonicClementsDecomposition`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-clements-decomposition#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicClementsDecomposition \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicClementsDecomposition\") (nakarehistro bilang `ModeRotation.Clements`). Pagpili iyon ng preset at hindi requirement ng framework: ibinababa ng isang susunod na seksyon ang parehong gate nang walang anumang decomposition. Hindi ine-exponentiate ng decomposition ang buong generator sa isang hakbang. Una nitong fina-factorize ang unitary sa hanggang $M(M-1)/2$ na mga rotation sa pagitan ng *magkatabing* mode kasama ang $M$ na single-mode phase, ayon sa rectangular mesh ni Clements et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id2). Ang bawat factor ay nagiging atomic na [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, na ima-map ng boson-to-qubit stage tulad ng iba pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The factorization itself is [`givens_decomposition()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/linalg-givens-decomposition#qiskit_bosons.linalg.givens_decomposition \"qiskit_bosons.linalg.givens_decomposition\"), which the decomposition calls. The map from a unitary to the many-body rotation is a group homomorphism, so the product of the factor rotations exactly equals the full rotation on the untruncated space. The mesh therefore adds no error of its own. Its benefit is locality. Each emitted evolution involves only the Pauli terms of the two modes it mixes (or of one mode for a phase), instead of terms across all modes.\n"
msgstr "Ang factorization mismo ay [`givens_decomposition()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/linalg-givens-decomposition#qiskit_bosons.linalg.givens_decomposition \"qiskit_bosons.linalg.givens_decomposition\"), na tinatawag ng decomposition. Ang mapa mula sa isang unitary papunta sa many-body rotation ay isang group homomorphism, kaya ang product ng mga factor rotation ay eksaktong katumbas ng buong rotation sa untruncated na espasyo. Kaya walang dagdag na error mula sa mesh mismo. Ang benepisyo nito ay locality. Bawat inilalabas na evolution ay may kinalaman lang sa mga Pauli term ng dalawang mode na hinahalo nito (o ng isang mode para sa phase), sa halip na mga term sa lahat ng mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile a random three-mode rotation and inspect what the pipeline emitted. A generic $3 \\times 3$ unitary needs the maximum of three rotations, plus three phases, and every factor is its own [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). All of them are declared on the whole register, but the operators inside act on a few qubits only:\n"
msgstr "I-transpile ang isang random na three-mode rotation at tingnan kung ano ang inilabas ng pipeline. Ang isang generic na $3 \\times 3$ unitary ay nangangailangan ng maximum na tatlong rotation, dagdag ang tatlong phase, at bawat factor ay sarili nitong [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). Lahat sila ay idineklara sa buong register, pero ang mga operator sa loob ay kumikilos sa kakaunting qubit lang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With three levels per mode, every mode occupies three qubits. A beamsplitter between two modes touches the six qubits of those modes, and a phase touches the qubits of one mode.\n"
msgstr "Sa tatlong level bawat mode, bawat mode ay gumagamit ng tatlong qubit. Ang beamsplitter sa pagitan ng dalawang mode ay humahawak sa anim na qubit ng mga mode na iyon, at ang phase ay humahawak sa mga qubit ng isang mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The factors are exact only once each evolution is synthesized well. The terms of a beamsplitter generator do not commute, so the default single-step product formula leaves an error in every factor. Pass a product formula with more repetitions to the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") plugin that maps the factors to reduce it:\n"
msgstr "Eksakto lang ang mga factor kapag maayos ang synthesis ng bawat evolution. Hindi nagko-commute ang mga term ng generator ng beamsplitter, kaya ang default na single-step na product formula ay nag-iiwan ng error sa bawat factor. Magpasa ng product formula na may mas maraming repetition sa plugin na [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") na nagma-map ng mga factor para mabawasan ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single boson entering mode 0 leaves in mode $j$ with probability $|U_{j0}|^2$. Compare the synthesized circuit with that exact result for increasing repetition counts. Decompose the circuit first so that the product formula is applied; without it, an exact simulator such as [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) applies the gate as its full exponential and hides the error.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang boson na pumapasok sa mode 0 ay lalabas sa mode $j$ na may probability na $|U_{j0}|^2$. Ihambing ang na-synthesize na circuit sa eksaktong resultang iyon para sa dumaraming bilang ng repetition. I-decompose muna ang circuit para maipatupad ang product formula; kung hindi, ang isang exact simulator gaya ng [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) ay ipapatupad ang gate bilang buong exponential nito at itatago ang error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error falls by a factor of about four for every fourfold increase in repetitions, as expected for a first-order formula. The cost grows in proportion, because every factor is repeated.\n"
msgstr "Bumababa ang error nang humigit-kumulang apat na beses sa bawat apat na beses na pagtaas ng repetition, gaya ng inaasahan sa isang first-order na formula. Proporsyonal na lumalaki ang gastos, dahil inuulit ang bawat factor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mode-rotation-direct-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lower a rotation without decomposing it {#lower-a-rotation-without-decomposing-it}"
msgstr "Ibaba ang isang rotation nang hindi ito dine-decompose {#lower-a-rotation-without-decomposing-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A decomposition in bosonic space is one way to lower a rotation. (The library does not include another way, but the boson-to-qubit stage does not depend on it.) [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") looks a plugin up by the name of the gate, and a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") that was left whole reaches it like any other gate. A plugin for it maps the generator of [`ModeRotation.to_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator\") in one go and emits a single [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) at unit time. That is all of it:\n"
msgstr "Ang decomposition sa bosonic space ay isang paraan para ibaba ang isang rotation. (Walang ibang paraan sa library, pero hindi umaasa rito ang boson-to-qubit stage.) Hinahanap ng [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") ang isang plugin ayon sa pangalan ng gate, at ang isang [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") na iniwang buo ay umaabot dito tulad ng ibang gate. Ang plugin para dito ay nagma-map ng generator ng [`ModeRotation.to_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation.to_operator\") nang sabay-sabay at naglalabas ng iisang [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) sa unit time. Iyon na ang lahat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Register it for the name of the gate in a pass manager that does not decompose it:\n"
msgstr "I-register ito para sa pangalan ng gate sa isang pass manager na hindi nagde-decompose nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rotation is now one evolution over all nine qubits, where the mesh has six, of which none spans more than six. The two are not the same approximation. The truncation is applied once to the generator of the whole rotation here, and to every factor separately in the mesh (hence the warning on the cutoff above). The direct path equals [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") of the operator at any cutoff, so it is the reference to compare a mesh against. What it costs is locality: its terms span all modes, and a product formula has more of them to subdivide.\n"
msgstr "Ang rotation ay isa nang evolution sa lahat ng siyam na qubit, samantalang ang mesh ay may anim, na wala ni isang sumasaklaw sa higit sa anim. Hindi magkapareho ang dalawang approximation. Ang truncation ay inilalapat nang isang beses sa generator ng buong rotation dito, at sa bawat factor nang hiwalay sa mesh (kaya ang babala tungkol sa cutoff sa itaas). Ang direktang landas ay katumbas ng [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") ng operator sa anumang cutoff, kaya ito ang reference na pagkukumparahan ng isang mesh. Ang kapalit nito ay locality: ang mga term nito ay sumasaklaw sa lahat ng mode, at mas maraming term ang kailangang hatiin ng isang product formula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neither is better in general, which is the reason to keep the choice open. Write a plugin like this one to compare lowerings, to use an encoding-specific rotation, or to hand the gate to something that understands it natively.\n"
msgstr "Walang mas mabuti sa pangkalahatan, kaya nga bukas ang pagpili. Sumulat ng plugin na tulad nito para ihambing ang mga lowering, gumamit ng encoding-specific na rotation, o ipasa ang gate sa isang bagay na nakakaintindi nito nang native.\n"

